    "body": "## What\n\nI've built and published a set of SDK packages that implement the BitChat binary\nprotocol and Nostr transport layer:\n\n### npm ([protocol-core](https://github.com/bitchat-sdk/protocol-core-js) · [nostr](https://github.com/bitchat-sdk/nostr-js))\n```sh\nnpm install @bitchat-sdk/protocol-core  # Binary encode/decode, TLV codec, peer ID utils\nnpm install @bitchat-sdk/nostr           # Nostr relay client, NIP-17 gift wrap, packet embedding\n```\n\n### PyPI ([protocol-core](https://github.com/bitchat-sdk/protocol-core-py) · [nostr](https://github.com/bitchat-sdk/nostr-py))\n```sh\npip install bitchat-protocol  # Binary encode/decode, TLV codec, peer ID utils\npip install bitchat-nostr     # Nostr relay client, NIP-17 gift wrap, packet embedding\n```\n\n### Swift Package Manager ([BitchatProtocol](https://github.com/bitchat-sdk/BitchatProtocol) · [BitchatNostr](https://github.com/bitchat-sdk/BitchatNostr))\n```swift\n.package(url: \"https://github.com/bitchat-sdk/BitchatProtocol\", from: \"0.1.0\")  // Binary codec\n.package(url: \"https://github.com/bitchat-sdk/BitchatNostr\", from: \"0.1.0\")     // Nostr integration\n```\n\nAll packages are wire-compatible with the current BitChat iOS and Android apps.\nThey're tested against a shared golden vector fixture suite that verifies\nencode/decode parity across all three languages.\n\n## What's included\n\n- Protocol v1 and v2 header support\n- Compression (raw deflate) with bomb detection\n- TLV codec for AnnouncementPacket and PrivateMessagePacket\n- NIP-17 gift wrap (seal → wrap → send, receive → unwrap → unseal)\n- Relay client with reconnect, observability hooks, and metrics counters\n- 100+ tests per language (unit, fixtures, fuzz)\n- Cross-language golden vector fixtures\n- CI workflow (GitHub Actions) for JS (Node 18/20/22), Python (3.10-3.12), Swift (5.9/5.10)\n\n## What I'm proposing\n\nI'd like to contribute these as an official part of the BitChat project — either as:\n\n1. **A directory in this repo** (e.g. `ecosystem/packages/`) with its own CI job, or\n2. **A separate repo** under the permissionlesstech org (e.g. `permissionlesstech/bitchat-sdk`)\n\nHappy to do either. The packages are self-contained, don't touch any existing code,\nand I'll maintain them going forward (tracking protocol changes and publishing updates).\n\nOpen to feedback on the approach before I put up a PR.",
